   <text:p text:style-name="P60"><text:span text:style-name="T5">(영영사전 뜻</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">)</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P52">'Receipt' refers to a written document confirming that money has been paid or goods have been received. Receipt shows proof of payment or delivery. People notice a document confirming a transaction. It is a noun. For example, 'Keep your receipt in case you need to return the item' means the document proving you paid for it.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="114" draw:name="가로선 59" draw:style-name="gr4" draw:text-style-name="P24" svg:x1="0.879cm" svg:y1="0.097cm" svg:x2="7.187cm" svg:y2="0.097cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>영수증 / 수령 / 받음</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54">receipt</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">영수증 / 수령 / 받음</text:p>
