   <text:p text:style-name="P60"><text:span text:style-name="T5">(영영사전 뜻</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">)</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P52">'Luggage' refers to bags and suitcases that a traveler carries. Luggage shows travel bags and cases. People notice the bags someone brings on a trip. It is a noun. For example, 'She checked her luggage at the airport before boarding' means her bags were registered and stored in the aircraft.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="126" draw:name="가로선 71" draw:style-name="gr4" draw:text-style-name="P24" svg:x1="0.879cm" svg:y1="0.097cm" svg:x2="7.187cm" svg:y2="0.097cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>짐 / 여행 가방</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54">luggage</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">짐 / 여행 가방</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P56"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="128" draw:name="가로선 73" draw:style-name="gr5" draw:text-style-name="P31" svg:x1="0.847cm" svg:y1="0.237cm" svg:x2="7.155cm" svg:y2="0.237cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>제 짐이 무겁습니다.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57">My luggage is heavy.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P58">제 짐이 무겁습니다.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P34">The flight attendant smiled kindly.</text:p>
