   <text:p text:style-name="P60"><text:span text:style-name="T5">(영영사전 뜻</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">)</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P52">'Attendant' refers to a person who assists or serves others in a specific place. Attendant shows serving person. People notice someone whose job is to help. It is a noun. For example, 'The flight attendant served drinks' means the person whose job is to help passengers on the plane.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="130" draw:name="가로선 75" draw:style-name="gr4" draw:text-style-name="P24" svg:x1="0.879cm" svg:y1="0.097cm" svg:x2="7.187cm" svg:y2="0.097cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>종업원 / 승무원</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54">attendant</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">종업원 / 승무원</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P56"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="132" draw:name="가로선 77" draw:style-name="gr5" draw:text-style-name="P31" svg:x1="0.847cm" svg:y1="0.237cm" svg:x2="7.155cm" svg:y2="0.237cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>승무원이 친절하게 미소 지었어요.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57">The flight attendant smiled kindly.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P58">승무원이 친절하게 미소 지었어요.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P34">She picked up a travel brochure at the airport.</text:p>
