     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame>merchandise</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P59"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="139" draw:name="가로선 84" draw:style-name="gr4" draw:text-style-name="P24" svg:x1="0.879cm" svg:y1="0.097cm" svg:x2="7.187cm" svg:y2="0.097cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P60"><text:span text:style-name="T5">(영영사전 뜻</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">)</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P52">'Merchandise' refers to goods that are bought and sold. Merchandise shows tradeable goods. People notice products available for purchase. It is a noun. For example, 'The store had a wide range of merchandise on display' means many different types of goods available to buy.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P53"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="138" draw:name="가로선 83" draw:style-name="gr4" draw:text-style-name="P24" svg:x1="0.879cm" svg:y1="0.097cm" svg:x2="7.187cm" svg:y2="0.097cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>상품 / 물품</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P54">merchandise</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P55">상품 / 물품</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P56"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="140" draw:name="가로선 85" draw:style-name="gr5" draw:text-style-name="P31" svg:x1="0.847cm" svg:y1="0.237cm" svg:x2="7.155cm" svg:y2="0.237cm">
     <text:p/>
    </draw:line>그 가게는 매주 새로운 상품을 판매합니다.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P57">The store sells new merchandise every week.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P58">그 가게는 매주 새로운 상품을 판매합니다.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P34">My magazine subscription expires next month.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P10"><draw:line text:anchor-type="paragraph" draw:z-index="30" draw:name="가로선 114" draw:style-name="gr1" draw:text-style-name="P11" svg:x1="3.109cm" svg:y1="0.23cm" svg:x2="4.248cm" svg:y2="0.23cm">
